Stephen Graves and David Simchi-Levi. Supply Chain Planning, MIT 15.762J/ESD.267J/1.273J, Spring 2011, graduate. [Programme](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-762j-supply-chain-planning-spring-2011/) · [Readings](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-762j-supply-chain-planning-spring-2011/pages/readings/) · [Assignments](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-762j-supply-chain-planning-spring-2011/pages/assignments/).

Complete the available published work on coordinated decisions, pooling, inventory placement and information across a supply network. Obtain assigned commercial cases/books through authorized access; where unavailable, explicitly identify the missing case and develop a documented chemical case using the open technical sources rather than pretending to have read it.

Instructors, graduate level, date and public assignment/reading structure were verified on 29 October 2026. The site does not supply all lecture content or solutions. OCW materials use CC BY-NC-SA subject to component exceptions; separate books and case studies are not included in that licence. Nothing is mirrored.

